    {
      "id": "818039cdff184d27b1aba93ccf624983",
      "owner": "ecl_smith_a",
      "created": 1784628636000,
      "modified": 1785756100000,
      "guid": null,
      "name": null,
      "title": "ANPG Block Data & Infrastructure Explorer",
      "type": "Web Experience",
      "typeKeywords": [
        "EXB Experience",
        "JavaScript",
        "lastEditor:ecl_abuelella_e",
        "modified: 1785755290138",
        "publishVersion:1.21.0",
        "Ready To Use",
        "status: Published",
        "template:jewelrybox",
        "version:1.21.0",
        "Web Application",
        "Web Experience",
        "Web Mapping Application",
        "Web Page",
        "Web Site"
      ],
      "description": "<h3><strong>Key Features &amp; Capabilities</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Dynamic E&amp;P Spatial Filtering:</strong> Quick-filter spatial data by asset hierarchy (<strong>Block</strong>, <strong>Prospect</strong>, <strong>Field</strong>).</li><li><strong>Seismic Data Management:</strong> Interactive visualization of 2D, 3D, and 4D seismic survey coverage and labels.</li><li><strong>Infrastructure Mapping:</strong> Asset tracking for offshore and onshore infrastructure, including <strong>Ports</strong>, <strong>FPSO units</strong>, facilities, and pipeline networks.</li><li><strong>Geological Context:</strong> Layer control for basin structures, including Sedimentary Basins, Onshore Basins, and local geological formations (<i>e.g., Kassanje, Etosha-Okavango</i>).</li><li><strong>Data Request Integration:</strong> Embedded <strong>Expression of Interest (EOI)</strong> workflows enabling users to submit requests for specific technical datasets.</li><li><strong>Analytical Summary Widgets:</strong> Integrated business intelligence widgets, including interactive chart visualizations for well status distributions (<i>e.g., Active, Closed, Abandoned, Dry, Gas</i>).</li></ul><h3><strong>Target Audience</strong></h3><ul><li>Exploration Geoscientists &amp; Geophysicists</li><li>Energy Sector Data Analysts &amp; GIS Specialists</li><li>Commercial Asset Evaluators &amp; Investors</li><li>Resource Management Authorities</li></ul>",
      "tags": [
        "BLOCKS",
        "SEISMIC2D",
        "SEISMIC3D",
        "FIELDS_AND_DAs",
        "SEISMIC4D",
        "WELLS",
        "ANGOLA",
        "ANPG"
      ],
      "snippet": "The ANPG Block Data & Infrastructure Explorer is an interactive, web-based geospatial dashboard designed for the exploration and management of petroleum, geological, and infrastructure datasets across Angola's onshore and offshore basins. It enables technical, commercial, and scientific stakeholders to evaluate Exploration & Production (E&P) assets in a centralized spatial interface.",
      "thumbnail": "thumbnail/thumbnail1785755418250.png",
      "documentation": null,
      "extent": [],
      "categories": [
        "/Categories/Culture (Infrastructure)/Surface installations",
        "/Categories/Surveys/Seismic survey extent",
        "/Categories/Environment/Soils and geology",
        "/Categories/Surveys/Seismic survey navigation lines",
        "/Categories/Culture (Infrastructure)/Pipelines"
      ],
      "spatialReference": null,
      "accessInformation": "We gratefully acknowledge the Ag\u00eancia Nacional de Petr\u00f3leo, G\u00e1s e Biocombust\u00edveis (ANPG) for providing access to the spatial datasets, concession block information, and exploration metadata represented in the Block Data & Infrastructure Explorer.",
      "classification": null,
      "licenseInfo": "<h2>Terms of Use (Demonstration Version)</h2><p>By accessing and viewing the <strong>ANPG Block Data &amp; Infrastructure Explorer</strong>, you acknowledge and agree to the following terms:</p><h3>1. Non-Official &amp; Demonstration Purpose</h3><ul><li><strong>Demo Use Only:</strong> This application is a non-official technical demonstration hosted by <strong>Exprodat</strong> to showcase web GIS visualization capabilities, data integration, and user-interface design within the energy sector.</li><li><strong>Not an Official Portal:</strong> This web map is <strong>not</strong> an official distribution channel or representative portal of the <strong>Ag\u00eancia Nacional de Petr\u00f3leo, G\u00e1s e Biocombust\u00edveis (ANPG)</strong>.</li></ul><h3>2. Data Source &amp; Intellectual Property</h3><ul><li><strong>Data Ownership:</strong> All spatial layers, block boundaries, seismic footprints, and well records shown are based on reference data sourced from <strong>ANPG</strong> and public geospatial repositories. ANPG and its licensors retain all intellectual property rights to the underlying data.</li><li><strong>Platform Hosting:</strong> The application architecture, GIS web services, and hosting infrastructure are managed by <strong>Exprodat</strong> using <strong>Esri ArcGIS Experience Builder</strong>.</li></ul><h3>3. Expression of Interest (EOI) Functionality</h3><ul><li>The <i>Expression of Interest (EOI)</i> form included in this application is configured for <strong>demonstration and workflow testing purposes only</strong>.</li><li>Submitting a request through this interface will not trigger official dataset licensing, commercial evaluations, or data delivery from ANPG or Exprodat.</li></ul><h3>4. No Warranty &amp; Limitation of Liability</h3><ul><li><strong>Provided \"As Is\":</strong> All map layers, spatial locations, and summary charts are provided strictly <i>\"as is\"</i> without any express or implied warranties regarding accuracy, completeness, or currency.</li><li><strong>No Commercial or Operational Use:</strong> Information displayed in this demo should <strong>not</strong> be used for formal decision-making, legal boundary determination, commercial asset acquisition, or operational planning. Neither Exprodat nor ANPG assumes liability for actions taken based on the contents of this demo app.</li></ul>",
